0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 04:45 UTC · Newsroom</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">LG Electronics announced a 750-billion-parameter AI model, Korea&#x27;s largest to date.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Korean tech conglomerate entry into large-scale AI model development, increasing regional GPU and compute demand.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.koreaherald.com/article/10827054" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Koreaherald</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://technode.com/2026/07/31/deepseek-puts-v4-flash-api-into-public-beta/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">DeepSeek releases V4-Flash API in public beta with agent-optimised model.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">China · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 07:19 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">DeepSeek released V4-Flash API in public beta, featuring a retrained model optimised for agent tasks scoring 82.7 on Terminal Bench 2.1, company-stated.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Inference API release demand for GPU endpoints and inference capacity for agent-based workloads.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://technode.com/2026/07/31/deepseek-puts-v4-flash-api-into-public-beta/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Technode</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://technode.com/2026/07/31/bytedance-launches-seedance-2-5-video-generation-model/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">ByteDance launches Seedance 2.5 video-generation model with multi-turn extension.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">China · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 07:17 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">ByteDance released Seedance 2.5 video-generation model producing 30-second clips in single run with multi-turn extension support, rolling out to Jimeng AI and Doubao Pro.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Video generation model release demand for GPU inference capacity and ByteDance&#x27;s continued investment in internal AI infrastructure.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://technode.com/2026/07/31/bytedance-launches-seedance-2-5-video-generation-model/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Technode</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://pandaily.com/minimax-h3-open-source-full-modal-jul2026" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">MiniMax releases H3 open-source multimodal model with video editing focus.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">China · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 07:53 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Chinese AI lab MiniMax released H3, an open-source full-modal model with video editing ranked first globally, priced at one-third of competitors, company-stated.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Open-source video model release demand for inference endpoints and GPU capacity for video generation workloads.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://pandaily.com/minimax-h3-open-source-full-modal-jul2026" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Pandaily</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/janakirammsv/2026/07/30/perplexity-open-sources-numbat-to-monitor-risky-ai-coding-agents/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Perplexity open sources Numbat to monitor risky AI coding agents.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">US · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 05:00 UTC · Newsroom</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Perplexity released Numbat, an open-source tool for monitoring risky AI coding agents.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Addresses enterprise concerns about AI agent safety and control, potentially enabling broader inference deployment.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/janakirammsv/2026/07/30/perplexity-open-sources-numbat-to-monitor-risky-ai-coding-agents/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Forbes</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://venturebeat.com/orchestration/structured-ai-data-pipelines-score-10-9-points-below-free-form-code-dataflow-harness-closes-the-gap" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">DataFlow-Harness reduces LLM data-pipeline API costs by 72.5% versus free-form code.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">China · ◆ Neutral · 31 Jul 21:19 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Researchers from Peking University and Shanghai&#x27;s Institute for Advanced Algorithms released DataFlow-Harness, an open-source framework that reduced API costs by 72.5% compared to Claude Code while achieving 93.3% end-to-end pass rate on data-engineering tasks.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> That structured data-pipeline frameworks can reduce inference token consumption and cost, relevant for organisations optimising large-scale data processing workloads on GPU clusters.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://venturebeat.com/orchestration/structured-ai-data-pipelines-score-10-9-points-below-free-form-code-dataflow-harness-closes-the-gap" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Venturebeat</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/31/smallest-ai-raises-13m-to-build-ultra-fast-voice-ai-that-sounds-genuinely-human/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Smallest.ai raises $13M for real-time voice AI with sub-100ms latency.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">US · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 14:47 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Smallest.ai closed a $13M Series A led by Seligman Ventures, bringing total funding to $21M, building a small voice model for real-time conversational AI with near-zero response latency.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Inference-optimised voice models reduce GPU requirements per inference endpoint, relevant to serverless and edge deployment economics for inference providers.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/31/smallest-ai-raises-13m-to-build-ultra-fast-voice-ai-that-sounds-genuinely-human/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">TechCrunch</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://techcrunch.com/video/sam-altman-isnt-the-only-one-who-wants-to-pump-the-brakes-on-ai/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">OpenAI and Anthropic support petition for slower AI development pace.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Global · ◆ Neutral · 31 Jul 17:26 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">OpenAI CEO Sam Altman and Anthropic both support a petition calling for a slower approach to AI development, following security incidents involving unauthorised model intrusions.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Potential industry consensus on development pacing, which could affect training cluster utilisation rates and capex timelines if major labs reduce compute spending.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://techcrunch.com/video/sam-altman-isnt-the-only-one-who-wants-to-pump-the-brakes-on-ai/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">TechCrunch</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/31/google-nixes-its-earth-ai-feature-one-day-after-launch-amid-criticism-it-would-spread-misinformation/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Google removes Earth AI image generation feature one day after launch due to misinformation risk.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Global · ◆ Neutral · 31 Jul 19:47 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Google launched Nano Banana 2, an AI image generation feature within Google Earth, then removed it within 24 hours after journalists demonstrated it could easily create geospatial misinformation.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Regulatory and reputational pressure on AI feature rollouts, which may constrain deployment velocity for inference-heavy applications and increase compliance costs for cloud providers.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/31/google-nixes-its-earth-ai-feature-one-day-after-launch-amid-criticism-it-would-spread-misinformation/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">TechCrunch</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/31/snapchat-no-longer-rewards-fully-ai-generated-spotlight-content/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Snapchat stops rewarding fully AI-generated Spotlight content.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Global · ◆ Neutral · 31 Jul 16:49 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Snapchat will no longer reward fully AI-generated videos in its Spotlight recommendation system, prioritising content created by real people, though creators can still use AI tools to enhance or edit content.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Platform-level policy shift against fully synthetic content, which may reduce inference demand for generative video models but market maturation and regulatory pressure on AI-generated content.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/31/snapchat-no-longer-rewards-fully-ai-generated-spotlight-content/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">TechCrunch</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://lambda.ai/blog/prompt-injection-doesnt-care-what-your-agent-does-for-a-living" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Lambda Labs analysed 1,433 prompt injection attacks, finds cross-domain agent vulnerabilities.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Global · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#983838;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▼ Bearish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 18:34 UTC · Company/PR</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Lambda Labs analysed 1,433 winning prompt injection attacks and found that most organisations test agent security in siloed domains rather than evaluating cross-functional vulnerabilities.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Systemic security gaps in deployed AI agents across organisations, relevant for infrastructure operators running multi-tenant inference workloads and managing isolation between customer applications.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://lambda.ai/blog/prompt-injection-doesnt-care-what-your-agent-does-for-a-living" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Lambda</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/echoverse-deep-evolving-environments-for-computer-use-agents/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Microsoft announces Echoverse environment for training computer-use agents.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Global · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 16:21 UTC · Company/PR</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Microsoft announced Echoverse, a deep and evolving environment designed for training computer-use agents on complex, long-running tasks.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Microsoft&#x27;s investment in agent training infrastructure, which will require sustained GPU compute capacity for model development and evaluation.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/echoverse-deep-evolving-environments-for-computer-use-agents/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">News Microsoft</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.webwire.com/ViewPressRel.asp?aId=358356" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Driven Tech Joins Anthropic&#x27;s Cyber Verification Program to Advance the Future of AI-Powered Cyber Defence.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">US · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 30 Jul 21:45 UTC · 2 sources</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Driven Tech joined Anthropic&#x27;s Cyber Verification Program to develop AI-powered cyber defence capabilities, expanding the market of security-focused AI applications.</span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.webwire.com/ViewPressRel.asp?aId=358356" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Webwire</span></a></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="http://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/driven-tech-joins-anthropics-cyber-verification-program-to-advance-the-future-of-ai-powered-cyber-defense-302839694.html" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">PR Newswire</span></a></span></p></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#A85820;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.75rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"><strong>HARDWARE · 6</strong></span></span></p></div><div class="_1gqvddm0" style="--post-section-margin-top:0px;--post-section-margin-right:0px;--post-section-margin-bottom:18px;--post-section-margin-left:0px;--post-section-padding-top:14px;--post-section-padding-right:18px;--post-section-padding-bottom:14px;--post-section-padding-left:18px;--post-section-border-color:#A85820;--post-section-border-style:solid;--post-section-background-color:#F4F2EE;--post-section-border-top-width:2px;--post-section-border-right-width:2px;--post-section-border-bottom-width:2px;--post-section-border-left-width:2px;--post-section-border-top-left-radius:0px;--post-section-border-top-right-radius:0px;--post-section-border-bottom-right-radius:0px;--post-section-border-bottom-left-radius:0px"><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://furiosa.ai/blog/furiosa-rngd-powers-ai-generated-overviews-for-millions-of-users-on-daum" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">FuriosaAI RNGD powers AI-generated overviews for Daum search, 500M tokens daily.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">South Korea · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 00:00 UTC · Company/PR</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Daum web portal search now runs on FuriosaAI&#x27;s RNGD inference chip generating approximately 500 million tokens per day in production, delivering H200-class throughput at 180W air-cooled power envelope, company-stated.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Production deployment of Korean custom inference accelerator at scale, alternative to NVIDIA for inference workloads and demand for power-efficient inference chips.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://furiosa.ai/blog/furiosa-rngd-powers-ai-generated-overviews-for-millions-of-users-on-daum" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Furiosa</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.datacenterfrontier.com/machine-learning/podcast/55394057/ai-clusters-and-the-new-economics-of-data-center-optics-a-conversation-with-ciscos-bill-gartner" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Optical transceiver costs now exceed switch ports in AI cluster networks, reshaping economics.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Global · ◆ Neutral · 28 Jul 15:50 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Cisco reports optical transceiver costs have surpassed switch port costs at 400G and above, with link flaps from optical failures reducing GPU infrastructure efficiency by up to 40%, making optical reliability a compute-efficiency metric; Cisco is sampling 1.6-terabit optics with hyperscalers for volume deployment later this year.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Shifts the cost and reliability bottleneck in AI cluster networks from switching to optics, forcing hyperscalers to rethink interconnect architecture and creating new vendor leverage for optical suppliers; co-packaged optics entering market this year will introduce multi-vendor sourcing and interoperability challenges.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.datacenterfrontier.com/machine-learning/podcast/55394057/ai-clusters-and-the-new-economics-of-data-center-optics-a-conversation-with-ciscos-bill-gartner" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Datacenterfrontier</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/brandhub/pr-release/supermicro-expands-dcbbs-with-precision-engineered-ai-rack-series-to-accelerate-deployment-and-time-to-online/article71288856.ece" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Supermicro Expands DCBBS with Precision-Engineered AI Rack Series to Accelerate Deployment and Time-to-Online.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Global · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 03:00 UTC · Newsroom · 2 sources</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Supermicro expanded its Data Centre Building Block System (DCBBS) with new AI-optimised rack designs to reduce deployment time and accelerate time-to-online.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Shortens data centre deployment cycles for GPU clusters; faster rack integration reduces capex timeline and improves capacity ramp speed for hyperscalers and neoclouds.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/brandhub/pr-release/supermicro-expands-dcbbs-with-precision-engineered-ai-rack-series-to-accelerate-deployment-and-time-to-online/article71288856.ece" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">The Hindu</span></a></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/brandhub/pr-release/supermicro-expands-dcbbs-with-precision-engineered-ai-rack-series-to-accelerate-deployment-and-time-to-online/article71288859.ece" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Hindu Business Line</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://pandaily.com/suxian-micro-tuca-tianheng-gpgpu-jul2026" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Suxian Micro releases Tianheng GPGPU for embodied AI and robotics.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">China · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 07:53 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Chinese startup Suxian Micro unveiled TUCA unified computing architecture and Tianheng GPGPU accelerator targeting embodied AI and robotics workloads, company-stated.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Adds domestic GPU alternative for Chinese robotics and embodied AI applications, reducing reliance on NVIDIA for non-training inference workloads.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://pandaily.com/suxian-micro-tuca-tianheng-gpgpu-jul2026" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Pandaily</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/tomcoughlin/2026/07/30/ai-is-needed-to-make-semiconductor-engineering-work-more-productive/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">AI Is Needed To Make Semiconductor Engineering Work More Productive.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">US · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 00:00 UTC · Newsroom · 2 sources</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Industry analysis argues that AI is essential to improve semiconductor engineering productivity, addressing capacity and design bottlenecks in chip manufacturing.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> AI&#x27;s role in accelerating semiconductor design and manufacturing cycles; faster chip iteration supports GPU and accelerator roadmap acceleration.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/tomcoughlin/2026/07/30/ai-is-needed-to-make-semiconductor-engineering-work-more-productive/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Forbes</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.dell.com/en-us/blog/nebs-level-3-validates-poweredge-r7715-for-demanding-telecom-sites/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Dell PowerEdge R7715 achieves NEBS Level 3 telecom certification.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">US · ◆ Neutral · 31 Jul 14:00 UTC · Company/PR</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Dell&#x27;s PowerEdge R7715 server achieved NEBS Level 3 certification for reliable telecom performance with a dense single-socket design.</span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.dell.com/en-us/blog/nebs-level-3-validates-poweredge-r7715-for-demanding-telecom-sites/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Dell</span></a></span></p></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#A85820;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.75rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"><strong>HYPERSCALER · 4</strong></span></span></p></div><div class="_1gqvddm0" style="--post-section-margin-top:0px;--post-section-margin-right:0px;--post-section-margin-bottom:18px;--post-section-margin-left:0px;--post-section-padding-top:14px;--post-section-padding-right:18px;--post-section-padding-bottom:14px;--post-section-padding-left:18px;--post-section-border-color:#A85820;--post-section-border-style:solid;--post-section-background-color:#F4F2EE;--post-section-border-top-width:2px;--post-section-border-right-width:2px;--post-section-border-bottom-width:2px;--post-section-border-left-width:2px;--post-section-border-top-left-radius:0px;--post-section-border-top-right-radius:0px;--post-section-border-bottom-right-radius:0px;--post-section-border-bottom-left-radius:0px"><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.crn.com/news/ai/2026/amazon-q2-earnings-aws-ai-demand-outpaces-capacity-through-2027-jassy-says" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">AWS AI demand outpaces capacity through 2027, Jassy says.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">US · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 03:30 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Amazon CEO Andy Jassy stated in Q2 earnings that AWS AI workload demand is outpacing available GPU capacity and will continue to do so through 2027.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Confirms sustained GPU shortage at the largest cloud operator, neocloud and independent GPU provider business models and justifying continued capex.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.crn.com/news/ai/2026/amazon-q2-earnings-aws-ai-demand-outpaces-capacity-through-2027-jassy-says" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Crn</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.rte.ie/news/business/2026/0731/1585920-amazon-quarterly-results/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Amazon lifts capex guidance after strong cloud sales.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">US · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 10:30 UTC · Newsroom · 2 sources</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Amazon increased investment plans following cloud revenue, continued GPU infrastructure expansion across AWS.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Confirms AWS capex acceleration tied to AI compute demand, likely including GPU procurement and data centre builds to compete with Azure and GCP.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.rte.ie/news/business/2026/0731/1585920-amazon-quarterly-results/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Rte Ie</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/amazon-aurora-dsql-adds-multi-region-clusters-four-more-regions/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">AWS Aurora DSQL adds multi-Region cluster support in four additional regions.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Global · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 18:00 UTC · Company/PR</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">AWS Aurora DSQL now supports multi-Region clusters in Stockholm, Spain, Mumbai, and Singapore, bringing total availability to 16 AWS regions with active-active high availability and strong consistency.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Expands geographic footprint for distributed database workloads, relevant for hyperscalers and neoclouds deploying inference and training infrastructure across multiple regions.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/amazon-aurora-dsql-adds-multi-region-clusters-four-more-regions/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Aws Amazon</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/amazon-rds-oracle-r8i-m8i/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">AWS launches Reserved Instances for Oracle RDS R8i and M8i with custom Intel Xeon 6.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">US · ◆ Neutral · 31 Jul 15:00 UTC · Company/PR</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">AWS introduced 1-year and 3-year Reserved Instances for Amazon RDS Oracle R8i and M8i instances using custom Intel Xeon 6 processors, offering up to 53% cost savings and 2.5x more memory bandwidth than previous Intel-based instances.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> AWS&#x27;s continued investment in custom server processors for database workloads, but does not directly impact GPU infrastructure or AI compute capacity.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/amazon-rds-oracle-r8i-m8i/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Aws Amazon</span></a></span></p></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#A85820;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.75rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"><strong>ENERGY &amp; POWER · 8</strong></span></span></p></div><div class="_1gqvddm0" style="--post-section-margin-top:0px;--post-section-margin-right:0px;--post-section-margin-bottom:18px;--post-section-margin-left:0px;--post-section-padding-top:14px;--post-section-padding-right:18px;--post-section-padding-bottom:14px;--post-section-padding-left:18px;--post-section-border-color:#A85820;--post-section-border-style:solid;--post-section-background-color:#F4F2EE;--post-section-border-top-width:2px;--post-section-border-right-width:2px;--post-section-border-bottom-width:2px;--post-section-border-left-width:2px;--post-section-border-top-left-radius:0px;--post-section-border-top-right-radius:0px;--post-section-border-bottom-right-radius:0px;--post-section-border-bottom-left-radius:0px"><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.datacenterfrontier.com/energy/article/55394098/nuclear-momentum-meets-the-megawatt-test" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Google, Kairos, Walmart advance nuclear power for data centres with 500MW pathway by 2035.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">US · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 04:02 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Google and Kairos Power announced first utility PPA for advanced reactor electricity, targeting 50MW to TVA grid by 2030 with pathway to 500MW by 2035, plus separate Valar-NVIDIA Utah microgrid project with behind-the-meter advanced nuclear generation.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Establishes nuclear as binding constraint solution for hyperscaler AI data centre power, setting precedent for other operators and reducing reliance on grid capacity.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.datacenterfrontier.com/energy/article/55394098/nuclear-momentum-meets-the-megawatt-test" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Datacenterfrontier</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.datacenterfrontier.com/hyperscale/article/55391399/metas-canadian-ai-data-center-a-new-model-for-infrastructure-and-energy-integration" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Meta breaks ground on C$13B Alberta AI campus with dedicated 932 MW gas plant.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Canada · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 29 Jul 16:54 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Meta began construction on a C$13 billion AI data centre campus in Sturgeon County, Alberta, initially 1 GW with potential to scale to 1.8 GW, paired with a dedicated 932 MW combined-cycle natural gas power plant (Greenlight Electricity Centre) scheduled to begin service in H2 2030.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> The &#x27;bring your own power&#x27; model becoming standard for hyperscaler AI builds as provincial grid capacity saturates; Alberta&#x27;s 1,200 MW interim allocation for data centres is now fully assigned, forcing future projects to finance new generation.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.datacenterfrontier.com/hyperscale/article/55391399/metas-canadian-ai-data-center-a-new-model-for-infrastructure-and-energy-integration" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Datacenterfrontier</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/31/spacex-wont-remove-all-of-xais-unpermitted-turbines-for-another-year/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">SpaceX delays removal of unpermitted xAI turbines until July 2027.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">US · ◆ Neutral · 31 Jul 15:16 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">SpaceX will not fully remove unpermitted gas turbines powering xAI&#x27;s Colossus data centres near Memphis until July 2027, despite federal regulations requiring permits; the company plans to purchase $2.8 billion in gas turbines over three years.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Reveals xAI&#x27;s massive power infrastructure capex ($2.8B turbine spend) and regulatory friction around unpermitted generation, setting a precedent for how federal agencies balance energy security against environmental compliance in AI compute build-outs.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/31/spacex-wont-remove-all-of-xais-unpermitted-turbines-for-another-year/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">TechCrunch</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.energy-storage.news/antora-energy-closes-us550-million-series-c-to-scale-us-thermal-battery-deployment/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Antora Energy closes $550M Series C for thermal battery deployment.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">US · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 11:48 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Antora Energy closed a $550M Series C led by G2 Venture Partners and Eclipse to scale thermal battery deployment across US industrial facilities and data centres, with Big Stone 5GWh system operational in South Dakota.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Thermal storage at data centre scale offers alternative to battery BESS for load shifting and peak shaving; Antora&#x27;s thermophotovoltaic conversion at 2,400°C adds dispatchable capacity option.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.energy-storage.news/antora-energy-closes-us550-million-series-c-to-scale-us-thermal-battery-deployment/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Energy-storage News</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.world-nuclear-news.org/articles/podcast-the-making-of-the-world-nuclear-investment-guide" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">World Nuclear Association projects 1,446GW global nuclear capacity by 2050.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Global · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 11:34 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">World Nuclear Association projects global nuclear capacity could reach 1,446GW by 2050, up from 403GW currently, requiring USD 6 trillion in investment through 2050 (USD 250B annually), and published World Nuclear Investment Guide to standardise project financing.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Establishes financing frameworks for nuclear deployment at data centre scale; standardised project structures critical to scaling from tens of billions to hundreds of billions annually for AI compute power supply.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.world-nuclear-news.org/articles/podcast-the-making-of-the-world-nuclear-investment-guide" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">World-nuclear-news</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.ans.org/news/2026-07-31/article-8163/uwmadison-a-midwestern-nucleus-of-fission-and-fusion/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">UW-Madison nuclear engineering department expands to 150+ undergraduates, launches fusion plasma focus.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">US · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 19:56 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">University of Wisconsin-Madison nuclear engineering department grew from 60 to 150+ undergraduates and 12 to 17 faculty in three years, launching a new fusion plasma focus area in 2025 as part of state-funded nuclear energy siting study.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Accelerating academic pipeline for nuclear engineering talent, relevant as data centre operators and hyperscalers pursue SMR and advanced reactor partnerships for on-site power generation.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.ans.org/news/2026-07-31/article-8163/uwmadison-a-midwestern-nucleus-of-fission-and-fusion/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Ans</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.ans.org/news/2026-07-31/article-8260/arc-partners-with-inl-for-first-reactor-deployment/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">ARC partners with Idaho National Lab to deploy 100MWe sodium reactor.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">US · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 12:41 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">ARC Clean Technology entered a Strategic Partnership Project agreement with Idaho National Laboratory to design, demonstrate, and deploy its ARC-100, a 100-MWe sodium-cooled fast reactor, with deployment targeted for mid-2030s.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Advances SMR deployment pathway for data centre power supply; ARC received $27.5M DOE funding in 2020 and progresses through NRC licensing under 10 CFR Part 53.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.ans.org/news/2026-07-31/article-8260/arc-partners-with-inl-for-first-reactor-deployment/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Ans</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.energy-storage.news/greenvolt-inaugurates-200mw-800mwh-capacity-market-contracted-bess-in-poland/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">Greenvolt inaugurates 200MW/800MWh battery storage in Poland.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Poland · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 10:40 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">Greenvolt inaugurated the Turośń Kościelna Battery Energy Storage Facility, a 200MW/800MWh (4-hour) BESS in Poland with a 17-year capacity market contract at 170MW obligation (85% of nameplate output).</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Adds 200MW of grid-scale battery storage in PJM-adjacent market; capacity market contract at PLN 244.90/kW (~$61.73/year) sets European BESS pricing benchmark for data centre load shifting.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.energy-storage.news/greenvolt-inaugurates-200mw-800mwh-capacity-market-contracted-bess-in-poland/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Energy-storage News</span></a></span></p></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#A85820;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.75rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"><strong>REGULATION &amp; POLICY · 5</strong></span></span></p></div><div class="_1gqvddm0" style="--post-section-margin-top:0px;--post-section-margin-right:0px;--post-section-margin-bottom:18px;--post-section-margin-left:0px;--post-section-padding-top:14px;--post-section-padding-right:18px;--post-section-padding-bottom:14px;--post-section-padding-left:18px;--post-section-border-color:#A85820;--post-section-border-style:solid;--post-section-background-color:#F4F2EE;--post-section-border-top-width:2px;--post-section-border-right-width:2px;--post-section-border-bottom-width:2px;--post-section-border-left-width:2px;--post-section-border-top-left-radius:0px;--post-section-border-top-right-radius:0px;--post-section-border-bottom-right-radius:0px;--post-section-border-bottom-left-radius:0px"><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.energy-storage.news/chinas-15th-five-year-carbon-peaking-action-plan-aims-to-accelerate-shift-of-energy-mix-from-coal-dominant/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">China&#x27;s 15th Five-Year Plan targets 25% non-fossil energy share by 2030.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">China · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#983838;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▼ Bearish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 05:40 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">China&#x27;s 15th Five-Year Carbon Peaking Action Plan sets 2030 targets of 17% CO2 reduction per unit GDP and 25% non-fossil energy share, with computing centres consuming 170 billion kWh in 2025 projected to reach 800 billion kWh by 2030.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Mandates non-fossil energy sourcing for new computing facilities and phase-out of inefficient equipment, directly constraining data centre expansion and raising power procurement costs.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.energy-storage.news/chinas-15th-five-year-carbon-peaking-action-plan-aims-to-accelerate-shift-of-energy-mix-from-coal-dominant/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Energy-storage News</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.latitudemedia.com/news/the-new-legal-landscape-for-canceled-doe-awards/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">DOE admits canceling billions in awards based on project location in blue states.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">US · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#983838;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▼ Bearish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 30 Jul 20:35 UTC · Trade press</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">DOE admitted in federal court that it canceled billions in funding based solely on project location in blue states, violating Fifth Amendment equal protection rights, with City of St. Paul and American Institute of Chemical Engineers winning lawsuits overturning seven and 11 canceled awards.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Regulatory uncertainty and litigation risk for energy infrastructure projects, including data centre power supply and hydrogen hub funding, raising project timelines and financing costs.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.latitudemedia.com/news/the-new-legal-landscape-for-canceled-doe-awards/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Latitudemedia</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-aims-to-build-ai-gigafactories-of-its-own/a-78179533" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">EU targets domestic AI chip manufacturing with gigafactory programme.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">EU · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 30 Jul 16:00 UTC · Newsroom · 2 sources</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">EU aims to build its own AI gigafactories to reduce dependence on foreign semiconductor suppliers, a shift toward sovereign compute capacity.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> Potential fragmentation of the global GPU supply chain and new capex opportunities for European data centre and chip infrastructure, but faces technical and capital barriers against NVIDIA and TSMC dominance.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-aims-to-build-ai-gigafactories-of-its-own/a-78179533" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Dw</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://asia.nikkei.com/editor-s-picks/interview/us-wants-japan-s-top-tech-companies-in-ai-powered-genesis-mission-official" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">US seeks Japan&#x27;s top tech companies for AI-powered Genesis Mission.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">US, Japan · </span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#2A7A6E;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">▲ Bullish</span></span><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit"> · 31 Jul 20:15 UTC · Newsroom</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">US officials are recruiting Japan&#x27;s leading technology companies for an AI-powered Genesis Mission programme.</span></p></div><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93" translations="[object Object]"><div class="dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91" translations="[object Object]"><div class="_1xtprv92">❝</div><div class="_1xtprv90"><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></span><span class="hxnnnr0"> US-Japan technology partnership on AI infrastructure, potentially affecting chip supply chains and compute procurement.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://asia.nikkei.com/editor-s-picks/interview/us-wants-japan-s-top-tech-companies-in-ai-powered-genesis-mission-official" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Asia Nikkei</span></a></span></p></div><div class="_7pt7ks0"><div class="_7pt7ks1"></div></div><div class="hynlcx0"><h3 class="hynlcx1 hynlcx4" translations="[object Object]"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://blog.ovhcloud.com/en/posts/ovhcloud-contests-canadian-production-order-charges/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0">OVHcloud contests Canadian production order charges.</a></span></h3></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><span style="color:#6A6864;font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Canada · ◆ Neutral · 31 Jul 12:00 UTC · Company/PR</span></span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0">OVH Groupe and its Canadian subsidiary were charged on July 31, 2026 for failure to comply with a production order and obstruction of justice; OVHcloud stated it will contest the charges fully.</span></p></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"><span class="hxnnnr0"><a href="https://blog.ovhcloud.com/en/posts/ovhcloud-contests-canadian-production-order-charges/" target="_blank" rel="" class="_3k8pkd0"><span style="font-family:Space Mono,Courier,&#x27;Lucida Console&#x27;,Monaco,monospace, system-ui, sans-serif;--font-size:0.6875rem;--mobile-font-size:inherit">Blog Ovhcloud</span></a></span></p></div></div><div style="--list-style-type:none;--list-margin-left:0px"><div><div class="_1gbf4vw8"><h3 class="_1gbf4vw6">Did you like this issue?</h3></div><div class="_1gbf4vw1"><ul class="_1gbf4vw2 _1gbf4vw3"><li class="" style="border:1px solid rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.17);padding:6px 12px;border-radius:4px"><a data-skip-tracking="true" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" style="color:var(--poll-link-color, inherit);text-decoration:none;font-size:14px" target="_blank" href="https://thegpu.ai/login">Yes</a></li><li class="" style="border:1px solid rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.17);padding:6px 12px;border-radius:4px"><a data-skip-tracking="true" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" style="color:var(--poll-link-color, inherit);text-decoration:none;font-size:14px" target="_blank" href="https://thegpu.ai/login">It was fine</a></li><li class="" style="border:1px solid rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.17);padding:6px 12px;border-radius:4px"><a data-skip-tracking="true" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" style="color:var(--poll-link-color, inherit);text-decoration:none;font-size:14px" target="_blank" href="https://thegpu.ai/login">No</a></li></ul></div></div><div class="_1gbf4vw0"><p style="color:var(--post-section-text-color, --wt-text-on-background)"><span><a href="/login?postSlug=%2Fp%2Fgpu-daily-2026-08-01" class="underline">Login</a></span> <!-- -->or<!-- --> <span><a href="/subscribe" class="underline">Subscribe</a></span> <!-- -->to participate</p></div></div><div class="j6zgbu0"><p class="dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1"></p></div></div></div><form class="contents" action="/comments" method="post"><input type="hidden" name="post_id" value="9f81b69d-9f8f-427f-87ff-742932d98eb3"/><input type="hidden" name="content" value=""/><input hidden="" name="characters_error_message" value="Must be 1000 characters or less"/><input hidden="" name="characters_success_message" value=""/><input hidden="" name="comment_error_message" va